00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.000
The case on both sides is whether Google must open its search data to rival search engines

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:54.020
and AI companies under the Digital Markets Act, and whether that order should run while

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:54.880
Google fights it.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:01.080
In July 2026, the European Commission told Google to share rankings, the queries people type,

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.140
click through rates and how often answers are viewed.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.260
The commission's reason is competition with safeguards.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:12.920
It says anonymization protects users and that rivals, including firms such as Gopin AI,

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.360
can use the data to compete with Google search.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:21.220
It also says a user could summon a rival assistant by voice, for instance to book a taxi or

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:21.940
look something up.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:27.300
If the order stands, eligible search firms would get the data by January 2027.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:31.840
and Android changes meant to help users would follow by July 2027.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:33.740
Google's reason is privacy.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.960
It says the handover may break European privacy law

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.000
and put millions of users at risk.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:42.540
It is filed at the General Court, Europe's second highest court,

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.380
and asked that Luxembourg Court for an interim measure,

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.320
arguing serious harm if the order takes effect first.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.280
Google also rejects how far the Commission reads

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.480
the Digital Markets Act.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:55.880
Both sides are arguing an order Brussels has already issued,

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:58.040
and Google has formally contested.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.240
Next is the court on the challenge

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.480
and on the request to pause any handover.

